= Problem
Many university courses incorporate oral presentations as part of their coursework or exams, which differ from conventional assessable submissions.
Artemis currently does not provide dedicated support for presentations as part of its assessment workflow. Instructors therefore often use spreadsheets, personal notes, or other external tools to organize presentations and document assessment results. These disconnected workflows separate presentation-related information from the actual course environment.

Instructors currently need to define assessment criteria manually, document the results, and transfer grades themselves. This increases the organizational effort and reduces transparency for students. They may have limited insight into the grading process and often need to rely on manual communication with instructors to receive feedback or assessment results.